A||||5||PAUL88GT||Rubber gasket/seal supplier?||||1||
Z||000000||PAUL88GT||08-02-2000||06:06 PM||||Can anyone recommend a supplier(s) for the factory sunroof and GT trunk rubber gaskets?<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||08-03-2000||10:05 AM||||They were still available through Pontiac that last time I checked.<P>Are you replacing the seal because your's is torn up or because the roof leaks?  Most roof leaks are due to the sunroof glass mounting hardware not the rubber seal around the perimeter.  You can get all new bolts with integral seals and the hinge tabs for around $20 from Pontiac.<P>I had ordered a new sunroof seal to replace the one in my 85SE when Ed Parks said to try the hardware fix first.  That did the job.  No leaks in the last three years.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||PAUL88GT||08-03-2000||10:33 AM||||I have already replaced the sunroof tabs and washers and it still leaks a little. My gasket is degrading and it looks bad.<P>I guess I will order them from Chriswell Chevy.<P>Does anyone know what type of sealant to use when installing the new sunroof seal?<BR>TIA<BR>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||08-03-2000||01:27 PM||||Paul, last time I checked, George at the Fiero Shop had both of them -- his # is 510-732-9516<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||PAUL88GT||08-04-2000||05:04 PM||||Chriswell Chevy's prices:<P>Sunroof seal: $47<BR>Trunk seal: $72<P>Thanks TG. I will call the Fiero Shop.<p>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 08-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||08-04-2000||06:51 PM||||also, when I installed my sunroof seal and trunk seal I used a marine grade clear silicone sealant. Hey, I installed my boat windows with it so I knew it would be waterproof!!) -- also, when you replace the sunroof seal make sure you clean the area under it good -- there are two drain holes that need to be clear - one on each rear corner of the recess where the seal fits........same with the trunk seal -- drain holes in each corner -- these usally get filled up with gunk and you may not notice that they are there -- look for them, you'll be glad you did!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">                <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A><p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 08-04-2000).]||||reg||1
